==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Haniwanwan]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*7 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~40 seconds<sup>800f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Oldhorn]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Loris]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
**1 [[Haniwanwan]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use your attackers and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] to kill Haniwanwan then stall until all Sir Rels are dead. After hitting the enemy base, use [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relic Cats]] such as [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]], [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]], [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Future Cat]] and [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Uril]] to kill and slow down Oldhorn. Once Oldhorn is dead, the stage is won.

Loris is a minor inconvenience at worst, and is only there to Curse your units. This rules out [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]] and [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]], but not much else.

If you need more time or damage to kill Oldhorn, use something with Knockback like [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] and throw in units with high DPS such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]] and Awakened Bahamut Cat for extra DPS.

